    "title": "Oil prices fall, Brent at $104.59 per barrel",
    "text": "Oil Prices Fall, Brent At $104.59 Per Barrel\nFahad Shabbir\n(@FahadShabbir)\nPublished September 17, 2026 | 07:00 AM\nWORLD CAPITALS, (UrduPoint / Pakistan Point News / WAM - 17th Sep, 2026) Oil prices continued to decline in early trading on Thursday, extending losses from the previous session.\nBy 00:49 GMT, Brent crude futures fell US$1.24, or 1.2 percent, to $104.59 per barrel, while US West Texas Intermediate (WTI) crude futures declined $1.14, or 1.1 percent, to $101.29 per barrel.\nBoth benchmarks had fallen by around $3 per barrel at the close of trading on Wednesday.",
    "summary": "Oil Prices Fall, Brent At $104.59 Per Barrel Published September 17, 2026 | 07:00 AM WORLD CAPITALS, (UrduPoint / Pakistan Point News / WAM - 17th Sep, 2026) Oil prices continued to decline in early trading on Thursday, extending losses from the previous session. By 00:49 GMT, Brent crude futures fell US$1.24, or 1.2 percent, to $104.59 per barrel, while US West Texas Intermediate (WTI) crude futures declined $1.14, or 1.1 percent, to $101.29 per barrel. Both benchmarks had fallen by around $3 per barrel at the close of trading on Wednesday.",
